For:

data_in = 10101010

The UART sends the bits LSB first.

UART frame
Start   Data bits                  Stop
  0     0 1 0 1 0 1 0 1             1

So the serial tx output is approximately:

0 → 0 → 1 → 0 → 1 → 0 → 1 → 0 → 1 → 1
       Expected signals
| Signal | Expected behavior       |
| ------ | ----------------------- |
| `tx`   | Starts at 1 when idle   |
| `tx`   | Goes to 0 for start bit |
| `tx`   | Sends 8 data bits       |
| `tx`   | Goes to 1 for stop bit  |
| `busy` | 1 during transmission   |
| `busy` | 0 after transmission    |
              Simple waveform
              tx:
      Start   Data Bits                  Stop
        ↓          ↓                       ↓
